meta {
  name: Create Pending Registration
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/pending-device-registrations
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "serial_number": "{{edge3Serial}}",
    "endorsement_public_key": "-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\n…paste PEM with \\n escapes…\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----\n"
  }
}

docs {
  `POST /pending-device-registrations` — allow-list a device. Returns 201
  with the created entry.

  The server later matches `serial_number` + `endorsement_public_key`
  **byte-for-byte** (including the trailing newline) against what the
  device sends in `POST /register`, so paste the PEM exactly as read from
  the TPM:

  ```
  sudo tpm2_readpublic -c 0x81010001 -f pem -o /dev/stdout | openssl rsa -pubin
  ```

  (`| jq -Rs .` turns that into a ready-to-paste JSON string.)
}
